  <figure>
    <img src={`${base}/fig_distill_2.png`} alt="2D to 3D bootstrapping shortens the path to high-quality training data on HARRIS-15." />
    <figcaption><strong>Fig. 2.</strong> 2D&rarr;3D bootstrapping shortens the path to high-quality training data on HARRIS-15. Three paths are compared. The Direct (upper bound) path annotates dense ground truth over 6 calendar months and trains a 3D model on it. The Direct (lower bound) path does the same over 1 calendar month. The Bootstrap path annotates sparsely (10 min 2D), trains a 2D&rarr;3D model, and generates pseudo-GT, then trains the same 3D model on that pseudo-GT. Bootstrapping saves 1&ndash;6 months of calendar time and $25k&ndash;$125k of human-annotator labor at $25/h.</figcaption>
  </figure>
